{
  "kind": "DomainClaimBundleSemanticsCases",
  "specRefs": [
    "§6.3.2",
    "§6.3.3",
    "§7.3.10",
    "§7.5.1"
  ],
  "note": "Bundle-level semantics for the domain claim: (V3) original-byte signature/hash preservation across Layer-2 resolution; (V4) semantic-claim deduplication — identity equivalence, evidence-independent, conflict-fails-closed; the demos-gcr-domain method evaluated over AUTHENTICATED GCR evidence — the ten GE-n binding checks (context, substrate, inclusion-covers-sourceTx, finality, SB-2 write-authorization relation, record.account==claim, record.host==identifier, recordRef.contentHash==hash(record), record.proofUrl==derive(identifier), and GE-10 provenance: the record is the state sourceTx actually wrote), the three GF-n freshness rules (verifiedAt derived from evidence.recordedAt with anti-reissue; effective-window bound; recordedAt future-dating/positive-window sanity within recordedAtSkewToleranceSec), and the unavailability->indeterminate mapping; and (CR-1) the DACS-1 §6.3.2 step-6 control-binding rule — controlled use requires the presentation to verify under the exact ed25519 account bound in the GCR record, directly or via an authenticated, PRESENTATION-BOUND SR-1 linkage. Accounts are real Demos ed25519 shapes (64 lowercase hex, no 0x); the valid/control-positive account equals the signedBundle signing key. SB-1 (inclusion/finality/state-recovery), SB-2 (write-authorization relation — account-key vs node-key is an open question), SB-3 (recorded time), and the SR-1 control hook are modelled synthetically; the concrete Demos wire formats are not yet fixed and bind at the substrate profile. Pin-map convention: gcrGuardPins pins exactly one PRIMARY vector per rule id (GE-1..GE-10, GF-1..GF-3, CR-1). The following behaviours are vector-covered but deliberately NOT pinned: the availability->indeterminate cases (not-found / transport-error / record-unreadable), the GE-10 unestablishable-provenance arm (provenance-unestablishable), the GF-3 non-positive-window arm (enforced in derive_effective_window, no dedicated vector), and the SR-1 negative cases (sr1-negative-not-bound / sr1-negative-replay, asserted in test_control_binding_cr1). Signatures are precomputed from a public seed and verified with the runner's self-contained RFC-8032 code; no cryptography import.",
